            "text": "Eliminating an enemy player in *Call of Duty* depends on mastering the basic combat mechanics, your loadout, and your positioning. Here is a breakdown of how to get kills:\n\n### 1. Basic Combat Mechanics\n*   **Shoot them (Gunplay):** \n    *   **Aim Down Sights (ADS):** Always hold the aim button (Left Trigger on controller, Right Mouse Click on PC) before shooting, especially at medium to long range. This vastly increases your accuracy compared to \"hip-firing.\"\n    *   **Aim for the head/upper chest:** Headshots deal significantly more damage and lower your \"Time to Kill\" (TTK).\n    *   **Control recoil:** Most automatic weapons pull upward when firing. Gently pull down on your aim stick or mouse to keep your crosshairs centered on the target.\n*   **Melee Attacks:** \n    *   If you are close to an enemy, use the melee button (usually Right Stick click on controller, or 'E'/'F' on PC) for a fast, high-damage hit. \n    *   If you sneak up directly behind an enemy and **hold** the melee button, your character will perform an instant-kill \"Finishing Move.\"\n*   **Lethal Equipment:** \n    *   Use grenades (Frag, Semtex), proximity mines, or throwing knives to damage or instantly eliminate enemies, especially those hiding in rooms or behind cover.\n\n### 2. General Gameplay Tips to Win Gunfights\n*   **Check the Mini-Map:** When enemies shoot unsuppressed weapons, they appear as red dots on your mini-map. Use this to anticipate where they are coming from.\n*   **Use Cover:** Never run out in the open. Always move from cover to cover (crates, walls, vehicles) so you have somewhere to reload or heal if you take damage.\n*   **Pre-aim corners:** If you suspect an enemy is around a corner, aim down your sights *before* turning the corner rather than after.\n*   **Listen to audio cues:** Wear headphones to hear enemy footsteps, reloading sounds, and callouts, which tell you their exact location.\n*   **Adjust your sensitivity:** If you are having trouble staying on target, lower your look sensitivity in the settings menu until your aim feels smooth and controlled.",
